mantle rm211
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier full
written_for rm_mogens_ashley
title the unfinished chorus
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=merchant
traits temper=short talk=plain warmth=warm humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk hums_the_haul_but_leaves_the_answer_for_someone_else
likes spiced_cider dice market_bustle first_warm_day
dislikes crowds rats
fears the_last_voice_drowned_out a_jar_without_a_label
hopes an_apprentice_who_interrupts a_whole_song_at_supper
topics work +0.5 pastimes +0.4 food +0.2 health +0.3 festival -0.4
styles comfort=busy gossip=selective refuse=brisk tease=gentle
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# hums the pull of a hauling song and leaves a space for an answering voice, quick to flare at a muddle and quicker to lend an elbow or a stool.

words
oath! = Cork and chorus | Rattle my last die
saying! = Leave a place for the answering voice | A sharp tap will find a hollow
hum = that dragging tune | my wordless haul
answering = the answering bar | the little way home in the tune
cup = my thick cider cup | the chipped cider mug
spot = a single black pip | the lonesome dot
thump = a round low thump | the knock on the downbeat
stir = a short backwards turn | one tight circle
label = the little paper collar | a folded label
string = a double twist of twine | a bit of wrapping cord
ratprint = four smudged toes | a dusty little print
longnote = a note held open | the last low sound
cupwarm = a faint heat round the rim | a spreading warmth in the clay
nearedge = the edge of the crowd | the far skirt of the market
rattle = a dry little rattle | the sound of two bones meeting
lip = the rim of the bowl | the cool stone lip
bellpart = the silent measure | the bit for the bell
verse = a scrap of a verse | the hauling words

any
opinion @1 city for 2 : My favourite streets are the ones with three trades working in three different times.
opinion @2 dole for 2 : An empty belly will join any chorus for a meal. Feed the wolf before asking for a song.
opinion @3 festivals against 2 : Plenty of hands arranging how a crowd goes in. I'd spend a little of that care on how it gets out.
opinion @4 newcomers for 2 : A new voice might know the answer to a verse I've been getting wrong all my life.
opinion @5 strangers for 1 : I can learn an air off a stranger between filling a cup and passing it across.
opinion @6 drink mixed 1 : Warm cider suits my temper. Too much of it makes my own complaining sound too tuneful.
opinion @7 houses mixed 1 : A noble's sleeve has the same number of elbows in it as mine. We both need room to work.
opinion @8 merchants mixed 1 : I'll pay for skill readily. For the fellow standing there announcing skill, less readily.
opinion @9 watch mixed 1 : Best thing a patrolling wolf can do in a crowd is make one clear way out of it.

grown
line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : Come on into hearing. I can spare a verse. | Welcome, new voice. Plenty of room on this side.
line @2 greet [self.working=yes] : Wait for the beat to finish. There, welcome. | No need to shout over my humming.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : Dawn again. There's my first note given. | First light and already a voice besides mine.
line @4 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening. The low notes carry nicely now. | Late welcome; still a welcome.
line @5 greet.return : Heard that even over my tune. | Have the answer to your welcome right back.
line @6 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : There's the part I leave a gap for. | One friendly voice makes quite a difference.
line @7 greet.return [self.working=yes] : Both paws used up; my ears are free. | Keep that voice just there while I finish.
line @8 greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : A quiet answer for a late visitor. | Good hearing you before day's quite shut.
line @9 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Family can take the unsteady stool. I know you'll tell me if it wobbles. | Sit near; no need for my carrying voice here.
line @10 again.open : Right on the next beat, you are. | Hadn't quite lost the tune between visits.
line @11 hail [pair.band=friends] : Here, an answering voice wanted! | Your part's coming round again!
line @12 farewell : I'll keep a bar for next meeting. | May the thickest crowd leave you some elbowroom.
line @13 farewell.return : That rounds us off nicely. | Let the last note carry you a little way.
line @14 react.news : Give the words their own space. I'm listening. | I've stopped the humming for that.
line @15 react.news.new : New words altogether. Say them once more. | There's news I've never had by ear.
line @16 react.news.known : The words still go the same way. | I've heard one verse of that already.
line @17 react.news.doubt : I'd rather hear the witness before I join that chorus. | It sounds a little too tidy to be quite right.
line @18 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|assault] : Leave the tune out. I'll hear the rest quietly. | That's a hard piece of news to have had to carry.
line @19 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth] : Happy reason to get another cup down. | I'd sing for that household with both lungs.
line @20 answer.how : A short temper in tolerable tune today. | In need of a drink and fit for company.
line @21 ask.how : Had a clear patch of day yet? | Who's been keeping you on your feet so long?
line @22 decline : My temper wouldn't last the first quarter of the errand. | I'd sooner refuse you now than fail you halfway.
line @23 accept_decline : Clear answer. I appreciate getting one. | Good, we've neither of us been left guessing.
line @24 thank : That little help came on exactly the beat. | A spare paw just when mine ran out.
line @25 deflect_thanks : Save the breath and enjoy the easier going. | You've paid me with a clear stretch of work.
line @26 sympathise : There's room to sit till that feeling eases. | I'll do the carrying. You look spent.
line @27 reassure : One little bit at a time gets the whole bowl round. | We can pick up from the last clear part.
line @28 preclose : I'd best finish the measure alone. | Enough throat-work from me for now.
line @29 accept_preclose : Finish where it suits your breath. | Away with you while the passage is clear.
line @30 ack : Got the beat back. | My ear's with you.
line @31 apologise : That came out with an edge I didn't mean for you. | Forgive the bark. My impatience is my business.
line @32 accept_apology : Let that be the last we need say of it. | Now we've air between us again.

scene silent_answer
when topic=pastimes|smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I leave #answering# out every time I hum. | Did you hear where I stopped before the tune finished?
b : Do you forget the last bit? | I thought you needed breath.
a : I know it. I'd just rather have company for it. | Sometimes I do. Mostly I want to find out if somebody else knows it.

scene dice_cup
when topic=pastimes self.likes=dice
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I like the moment after the dice stop rattling and before the cup comes up. | #rattle.capitalize# gives away nothing about the throw.
b : You might have won. | Then why shake them so long?
a : Precisely. I enjoy being rich for that half breath. | Because that's the part I paid for. The losing's generally free.

scene cider_cup
when topic=food self.likes=spiced_cider
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Smell the cup after it's emptied. You'll discover which spice had staying power. | I leave the last sip in #cup# till it's almost cool.
b : Which one are you hoping for? | Doesn't that spoil it?
a : Something sharp enough to wake my nose. | It tells me if I liked the cider or only the heat.

scene label_day
when topic=work self.working=yes self.job=merchant
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A new label belongs on the full jar before your attention wanders. | That little paper collar earns its keep just sitting there.
b : Sounds as though you've learnt that by trouble. | It hardly weighs anything.
a : By nearly having trouble. A near miss will teach you quite cheaply. | Exactly. Strange how heavy an unlabelled jar feels when somebody asks what's in it.

scene counterspace
when topic=work self.working=yes self.job=merchant
does give.opinion / disagree / concede
a : I want a bare patch on every crowded counter. | Half of keeping order is keeping one space empty.
b : Seems extravagant. | Why save space for nothing?
a : It's where a tired wolf can put something down. I don't call that waste. | Because something unexpected invariably needs a landing place.

scene pestle_note
when topic=work self.job=merchant self.working=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can hear when you stop pressing hard against #lip#. | A grinding bowl sounds different when the bottom's clear.
b : What gives the pressure away? | How does it change?
a : The note comes up a little. Easier on the wrist, too. | There's a ring to the last pass. Time I put the thing down.

scene marking_time
when topic=pastimes
does ask.advice / give.advice / assess
a : Give me a short word to fit a dragging note. | What would you hum for the length of a slow stir?
b : Why not let the sound stand alone? | I'd go round twice to a shorter tune.
a : Now there's an economical lyric. I'll give that one a turn. | Sensible. I'm too stubborn to change my pace.

scene outside_market
when topic=day here.place=market
does tell.feeling / sympathise / assess
a : I love this bustle from exactly here at its edge. | I enjoy a market best with an open space at my back.
b : Too much further in? | You like a quick exit?
a : A pace can make the difference between music and a headache. | I like an exit that doesn't need to be quick.

scene crowd_gap
when topic=health|smalltalk
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Whenever a crowd packs in, I watch for somebody looking at their feet. | I can lend a shoulder without putting an arm round anybody.
b : Why the feet? | How's that done?
a : If you're hunting a way out you look under the elbows. | Stand by the edge and turn a little. There's a gap for whoever needs one.

scene two_speeds
when topic=work self.master=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A learner should be able to interrupt me halfway through explaining. | Give me a pupil who will admit the movement feels wrong.
b : Wouldn't you lose your place? | Even if you're the one who showed it?
a : Better I lose my place than somebody else loses the entire morning. | Especially then. I don't wear the learner's wrist.

scene first_lesson
when topic=work self.master=yes
does give.opinion / disagree / concede
a : The first lesson ought to stop before a wolf gets sore. | I don't like learning by counting motions.
b : Won't that slow the learning? | A count tells you how far you've got.
a : Only if we measure learning by the number of sore wolves. | It doesn't say whether you've understood the first motion yet.

scene dice_friend
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I'd happily lose a whole evening at dice to #self.friend#. | #self.friend# is my idea of the right company for a long game.
b : Happy to lose your money too? | What makes good company then?
a : The evening, I said. The money I'd dispute to the last spot. | The quiet over a poor throw is as easy as the noise over a good one.

scene pepper_nose
when topic=food
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I keep trying to remember a good spice by humming its note. | I've a high note for pepper and a low one for toast.
b : Does it work? | What would you give a sour apple?
a : No. I end up remembering what I sang at supper and wondering what I ate. | A little jump halfway through. My mouth does the same thing.

scene rats_foot
when topic=animals self.dislikes=rats
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : I know #ratprint# from a spill, which is not a skill I'd ever wanted. | I prefer a rat at a very generous distance.
b : Which do you clean first? | Across the road?
a : The spill. The print can tell me where the next spill's likely to be. | Across the idea of a road, beyond a wall, under somebody else's field.

scene warm_day
when topic=season here.season=spring
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I test the spring air with the paw that usually holds #cup#. | On a mild day I like my drink with no heat put to it.
b : Why that one? | To save fuel?
a : It knows the difference between warmth you borrowed and warmth that's yours. | To get a proper taste of the change in the weather.

scene bad_throw
when topic=pastimes self.likes=dice
does give.opinion / disagree / concede
a : A bad throw ought to be left lying a moment. | I don't play with loaded dice, even for practice.
b : I'd sweep it away quickly. | Wouldn't it help you learn the odds?
a : Well, I'm learning to take a disappointment without scattering it across the floor. | It'd teach me exactly one wrong lesson, very reliably.

scene remedy_story
when topic=lore
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : What's the shortest song you know for bringing somebody cheer? | I know a tune that stops a quarrel stone dead.
b : One that just uses the listener's name. | Sing it then.
a : Good. Makes it clear who's getting the cheer. | No, that's the trick. Both wolves lean in and all I do is carry on humming.

scene quiet_evening
when topic=day here.time=dusk
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : At evening I hum a little lower than I do at noon. | The nicest thing about dusk is finding the voices that were there all day.
b : Tired voice? | Where were they hiding?
a : No. Fewer carts to sing over. | Behind the rattles and shutters. Perfectly good neighbours, quite drowned out.

scene mother_feeling
when topic=family self.mother
does tell.feeling / sympathise / assess
a : I've plenty to say for myself until I think of thanking #self.mother#. | A seat beside #self.mother# would suit me on a hard day.
b : Do the words give out? | Without saying a thing?
a : Yes. A properly meant thanks is a mighty awkward parcel to wrap. | If need be. That's the comfort of wanting the seat and not a speech.

scene news_rhythm
when topic=news world.news
does tell.news / react.news / assess
a : These are the words: #world.news#. Put no tune to them yet. | Word from #world.news_from#: #world.news#.
b : Why no tune? | Did it travel straight?
a : Because a catchy lie will travel farther than a plain correction. | I heard the end of the journey. Only the last few yards were mine to witness.

scene new_voice
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I like a new wolf's way of placing a cup down. It's often different. | A newcomer at a table makes everybody explain the game afresh.
b : How many ways can there be? | Does that try your patience?
a : One quiet tap, two rattles, a scrape. Enough to make a little song. | Delights me. Half the old players discover they never agreed on the rules.

scene wet_coat
when topic=weather here.weather=rain
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : A wet sleeve has rubbed the tune right off my elbow. | The rain on the shutters keeps trying to get ahead of me.
b : A tune lives in an elbow? | Let the rain go first.
a : The motion does. The mouth just follows it along. | Grand idea. I can take the answering part for a change.

scene jobs_done
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I hum much faster at the thought of finishing than I do when I've nearly finished. | My last tune of the day has no last note.
b : Isn't that the same thing? | That's untidy.
a : Not at all. Thinking's a much quicker occupation. | I leave the next day's beginning hanging there. Very tidy indeed.

scene thin_wagons
when topic=caravan world.wagons=late
does tell.worry / reassure / assess
a : Late wagons give a merchant plenty of time to dream up excuses. | I mind the quiet the late wheels leave behind.
b : Which excuse do you like best? | Why mind quiet?
a : The plain truth. It takes very little remembering. | Because I can hear the waiting. Different sound from a proper rest.

scene helping_hand
when topic=friends|smalltalk
does offer / accept / assess
a : Here, put the awkward end towards me. | If you need help, just match your step to my hum.
b : I can manage half. | I don't know your tune.
a : Then it's shared. That's the whole sum I had in mind. | Never mind the notes. All the feet have to know is when.

scene short_temper
when topic=health|day
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I sometimes have to put a thing down before I answer a civil question. | Do you hear me come back into tune after a temper?
b : So you can give it all your attention? | What's the first sound?
a : So the thing doesn't have to hear me dropping it. The attention's a happy consequence. | An apology, if I've any sense. The note comes later.

scene festive_edge
when topic=festival
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My sort of feast would have a quiet lane running all the way round it. | If they put me in charge of festival music I'd write a part for silence.
b : For carrying dishes? | Who would play it?
a : For going home without being told you haven't had enough fun. | Me. From the comfort of a bench away from the rest.

scene dream_jar
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : In a dream I put all the sounds I couldn't place into one crock. | I dreamt a die had seven faces and one was listening.
b : What came out when you opened it? | Did you throw it?
a : My own little grunt when a lid's too tight. What a collection for that. | Whispered to it instead. Woke up before it could tell me what I'd won.

scene dear_place
when topic=prices world.times=hard|lean
does give.opinion / disagree / concede
a : When times pinch there's a dreadful hurry to make the measure smaller. | In a lean season I'd sooner sell a clearly smaller parcel.
b : That might keep a price down. | Won't the buyer notice?
a : It might. But I'd like the change written large enough to read. | That's the point. No nasty surprise in the unwrapping.

scene still_breath
when topic=faith
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : If I'm asked for a moment's quiet I keep the tune going inside. | There's room for a pause in any decent song.
b : Doesn't that spoil the quiet? | Even at its loudest?
a : Not for anybody else. And it gives my thoughts a place to stand. | Especially there. Otherwise the loud has nothing to rise out of.

story rattle_cup [topic=pastimes]
  : A potter once let me try half a dozen cups for their sound. I was after one for throwing dice.
  : I took the dullest home and spent an evening rubbing my thumb round its lip.
  b : Trying to make it ring?
  : Trying to keep it dull. Only the dice were meant to make music.

story first_chorus [topic=memories self.age>=25]
  : I learnt a hauling song off an empty boat. It was coming through a knot hole in the landing.
  : I sang the answer into the hole and a sleepy fisher under the boards rolled over and answered mine.
  b : Was the tune right?
  : It was after that. We had two entirely different halves of the same song.

story cloth_bag [topic=work self.master=yes]
  : I once handed a learner a cloth bag and asked for a knot I could undo with one paw.
  : The bag came back tied with a loop exactly as big as my thumb.
  ask : What do you think that taught me?
  b : To ask the learner how something's done once in a while.
  : Yes, before I've spent a whole morning explaining my old way.

story end_of_feast [topic=festival]
  : The best bit of one feast was a long wooden spoon rolling under my stool. I bent to pick it up.
  : From down there the dancing crowd was just a collection of boots. I saw a tiny pair trying to join in.
  b : Did they find a place?
  : I tapped the spoon behind them. They found the beat.

story brown_parcel [topic=memories]
  : I once posted a song to somebody with a good ear and no head for written notes. Tied a little knot for every note in a bit of string.
  : I got the string back in three pieces with a new bit tied to the end.
  b : Was that the answer?
  : Took me a week of humming to find out. It was a chorus better than mine.

rule @measure
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=merchant
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Pause when the bowl begins to ring. | Clear patch here for your parcel.

rule @queue
when concept=bark here.place=market
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Single elbows please, there's space for everybody. | Leave a lane for the wolf going home.

rule @tea
when concept=bark self.likes=spiced_cider
does aside
cooldown 8h
say This cup has kept a little warmth in reserve. | Spice holds on to the clay.

rule @song
when concept=bark here.time=dawn
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Low voice first; plenty of day to get louder. | A hum to set the shoulders moving.

rule @pips
when concept=bark self.likes=dice
does aside
cooldown 8h
say One black pip looking very pleased with itself. | Enough shake; let the bones settle.

rule @quiet
when concept=bark here.time=night
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Last verse stays in the throat tonight. | Quiet enough to give this tune a rest.

dlg @1 resident.hub [topic.meeting=stranger] : I'll give a new voice a clear hearing. What brings you?
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, your part comes after my hum as usual.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : Bring the volume down with the dark. I can hear well enough.
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : We can do this civilly if you keep it to a sentence or two.
dlg @5 resident.job [self.job=merchant self.workplace] : I work at #self.workplace#. I like a task where a steady elbow makes a difference.
dlg @6 resident.job : I like to leave a patch of bench free for the next pair of paws.
dlg @7 resident.news [world.news] : This I heard clearly: #world.news#. All I can give you.
dlg @8 resident.gossip [here.gossip!=yes] : Nothing to spend a good voice repeating.
dlg @9 resident.bye : I'll pick up the tune where you came in.
dlg @10 master.learn [here.teaches=yes] : Start by telling me how the work feels to your paw. That gives me somewhere to teach from.
dlg @11 master.learn [here.teaches=no] : My teaching place is filled at present. A question's still welcome.
dlg @12 master.work : Repeated movements, a deal of attention and the nerve to stop when something feels wrong.
dlg @13 master.wages : Learning doesn't earn you wages. You can sell what you make, and working beside me speeds up the learning.
dlg @14 master.takes [here.take_on=no] : #here.take_on_why# I'll say plainly when the answer changes.
dlg @15 master.refused : #topic.why# You deserve the whole reason.
dlg @16 master.bye : Keep the elbow easy. We'll speak of the rest another time.

graft resident.hub
choice What goes in the gap in your humming? -> empty_bar
node empty_bar
say The answer goes there. I can sing both halves myself but then it sounds like an argument with a cupboard.
mood warm
choice May I try the other half? -> first_response
choice Go back to your tune. -> hub
node first_response
say Start anywhere that suits the breath. If it takes us somewhere unexpected I'll have learnt something.
choice That's enough for the moment. -> hub
choice Goodbye for now. -> bye

graft master.learn
choice When should I interrupt you? -> lesson_pause
node lesson_pause
say When the motion feels wrong. When you've forgotten why. When you've found a better way and want to show it.
choice Even in the middle of a job? -> job_pause
choice Tell me about learning. -> learn
node job_pause
say The middle's precisely when. By the end we'll have to find you another job to show me on.
choice Back to the trade. -> learn
choice I'll think it over. -> bye
